{"name":"Ambrosia","hex":"#c6e1bc","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ambrosia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Asteraceae – ragweeds, of the Americas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ambrosia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ambrosia","blocks":[{"text":"In the ancient Greek myths, ambrosia is the food or drink of the Greek gods, and is often depicted as conferring longevity or immortality upon whoever consumed it. It was brought to the gods in Olympus by doves and served either by Hebe or by Ganymede at the heavenly feast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/WLANL_-_MicheleLovesArt_-_Museum_Boijmans_Van_Beuningen_-_Istoriato_schotel%2C_de_maaltijd_der_Goden_op_de_Olympus.jpg/330px-WLANL_-_MicheleLovesArt_-_Museum_Boijmans_Van_Beuningen_-_Istoriato_schotel%2C_de_maaltijd_der_Goden_op_de_Olympus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrosia","wikidata":"Q131409"},{"title":"Ambrosia (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Ambrosia is an American rock band formed in Los Angeles in 1970. Ambrosia had five top 40 hit singles released between 1975 and 1980, including the top 5 hits \"How Much I Feel\" and \"Biggest Part of Me\", and top 20 hits \"You're the Only Woman \" and \"Holdin' on to Yesterday\". In 1989, the group's original lineup reunited, and following the departure of guitarist and frontman David Pack in 2000, the group has been augmented by various singers and led by fellow founders Joe Puerta (bass/vocals) and drummer Burleigh Drummond. Original keyboardist Christopher North also performed with Ambrosia until his death in 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Ambrosia1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ambrosia1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrosia_(band)","wi